    kg:textSpan "perform on the given benchmarks. 3 Multimodal architectures Authors: Luyang Chu, Karol Urbanczyk, Giacomo Loss, Max Schneider, Steen Jauch-Walser Supervisor: Christian Heumann Multimodal learning refers to the process of learning representations from dierent types of input modalities, such as image data, text or speech. Due to methodological breakthroughs in the elds of Natural Language Processing (NLP) as well as Computer Vision (CV) in recent years, multimodal models have gained increasing att" .

