    kg:textSpan "inference tasks. However, in tasks such as imagetext retrieval, encoding the interactions of all image-text pairs leads to slow inference speed. The dual encoder employs separate single-modal encoders to encode the two modalities. After sufficient encoding, a simple dot product or shallow attention layer is used to calculate similarity scores between them, without relying on complex Transformer structures. The fusion encoder is suitable for inference tasks, while the Dual encoder is suitable for" .

