    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2412_19412_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "8 , 60 ]. To this end, we try to generate pseudo modalities to obtain a large-scale multimodal dataset, which may help to train a unified matching model for multiple cross-modal cases. Cross-modal generation from multi-viewed RGB images has distinct advantages. a) Cheap: Those RGB images are easy to collect, such as capturing from the internet [ 27 ] or video frames [ 41 ]. This allows us to avoid capturing raw multimodal images in the wild. b) Flexible: We can obtain any pseudo modality we want" .

