    kg:textSpan "of each visual token remain constant, while distinct IDs are assigned to the height and width components based on the tokens position in the image. When the input is video with audio, the audio is still encoded with identical position IDs for every 40ms per frame, and the video is treated as a series of images with temporal ID increments for each frame, while the height and width components follow the same ID assignment pattern as images. Since the frame rate in video is not fixed, we dynamicall" .

