    :hasEvidenceText "A multimodal model combines multiple data types, including images, text, audio, and more."^^xsd:string,
        "Any-to-Any Multimodal Models"^^xsd:string,
        "Having a single neural network to handle a wide and varied range of tasks and modalities has been a longstanding goal."^^xsd:string,
        "Having a single neural network to handle a wide and varied range of tasks and modalities has been a longstanding goal. Such a model, especially when capable of any-to-any predictions"^^xsd:string,
        "Having a single neural network to handle a wide and varied range of tasks and modalities has been a longstanding goal. Such a model, especially when capable of any-to-any predictions, brings notable advantages"^^xsd:string,
        "Multimodal learning refers to the process of learning representations from dierent types of input modalities, such as image data, text or speech."^^xsd:string,
        "While the system initially focuses on languages and images, it opens up possibilities for incorporating other modalities like videos or voices."^^xsd:string,
        "a model capable of simultaneously processing temporal and spatial dimensions for fine-grained multi-modal understanding tasks."^^xsd:string,
        "current multimodal models are primarily designed under the assumption of a one-to-one relationship between texts and image inputs."^^xsd:string,
        "demand integration of several multimodal capabilities for answering"^^xsd:string,
        "information from multiple modalities, these models are limited by their inability to perceive different modalities in a fully integrated way"^^xsd:string,
        "leveraging the scaling capabilities of LLMs into multimodal models."^^xsd:string,
        "models that can process and generate a"^^xsd:string,
        "multi-modal capabilities of MiniGPT-v2"^^xsd:string,
        "multimodal LLM (MLLM), which integrates a CLIP image encoder, LLM and a vision-language MLP projector to align image features to the input embedding space of the LLM."^^xsd:string,
        "our model is trained on multimodal pairs, which include various combinations of image and text modalities on both the query and target sides."^^xsd:string,
        "recent general-purpose multimodals models"^^xsd:string,
        "unified multimodal models. 3 ( FUDOKI ) is a Japanese term referring to ancient records that comprehensively document and integrate the culture, geography, and traditions of different regions."^^xsd:string,
        "using different learning objectives in combination can enhance the performance of multimodal models."^^xsd:string,
        "we list each models language tower, as this significantly impacts MLLM performance"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :model,
        owl:Thing ;
    skos:altLabel "Multimodal Model"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:skos_definition "A model architecture that integrates several multimodal capabilities for answering complex questions, often utilizing a language tower and a vision encoder."^^xsd:string ;
