    :hasEvidenceText "Contrastive learning performed across instances featuring disparate target modalities has the potential to introduce noise and give rise to negative effects"^^xsd:string,
        "Robinson et al. ( 2021 ) propose a hard negative sampling strategy where the user can control the hardness."^^xsd:string,
        "a caveat of contrastive learning is the requirement of a large number of negative samples."^^xsd:string,
        "a caveat of contrastive learning is the requirement of a large number of negative samples. These samples can be maintained in a memory bank"^^xsd:string,
        "the contrastive prediction task aims to identify x i in { x i } k = i for a given x i ."^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :entity,
        owl:Thing ;
    skos:altLabel "Contrastive Learning"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:skos_definition "A learning approach that requires a large number of negative samples to determine if features are from the same image or not."^^xsd:string ;
