    kg:textSpan "Multimodal Chain-of-Thought Reasoning in Language Models Zhuosheng Zhang zhangzs@sjtu.edu.cn School of Electronic Information and Electrical Engineering, Shanghai Jiao Tong University Aston Zhang az@astonzhang.com GenAI, Meta arXiv:2302.00923v5 [cs.CL] 20 May 2024 Mu Li muli@cs.cmu.edu Amazon Web Services Hai Zhao zhaohai@cs.sjtu.edu.cn Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Shanghai Jiao Tong University George Karypis gkarypis@amazon.com Amazon Web Services Alex Smola alex@smola.org Am" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2302_00923_rag__chunk_014> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2302.00923_rag::chunk_014" ;
    kg:docId "2302.00923_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2302_00923_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "7 Conclusion This paper formally studies the problem of multimodal CoT. We propose Multimodal-CoT that incorporates language and vision modalities into a two-stage framework that separates rationale generation and answer inference, so answer inference can leverage better generated rationales from multimodal information. With Multimodal-CoT, our model under 1 billion parameters achieves state-of-the-art performance on the ScienceQA benchmark. Analysis shows that Multimodal-CoT has the merits of m" .

