    kg:textSpan "multimodal video models with respect to fine-grained activity details, such as changing cut a ginger twice using a knife to cut a ginger three times using a knife . We construct negatives upon two granularities: word level and event level. Specifically, word level negatives denote the case where a certain word or phrase is replaced while event level negatives denote the case where the order of two events are reversed. Empirically, we find that LLMs can produce more creative and diverse negatives" .

