    kg:textSpan "crucial for understanding tasks. While Janus [ 57 ] attempts to address this conflict by employing separate encoders for understanding and generation tasks, this increases model complexity without fundamentally resolving the underlying representation disparity. These limitations underscore a critical gap in the field: the absence of a unified visual encoding mechanism that can effectively serve both perception and generation objectives. This motivates our central research question: Can one singl" .

