    kg:textSpan "is prohibitively expensive; For example, regular 16-bit fine-tuning of a LLaMA 65B parameter model [ 45 ] requires more than 780 GB of GPU memory [ 7 ]. Therefore, it is critical to reduce the memory footprint of LLMs/LMMs, especially when it comes to improve the accessibility of large models to a wider community. Parameter-efficient training is an effective approach for LMM adaptation. Two representative methods are illustrated in Figure 21 . They freeze most of the model parameters, and only a" .

