    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2404_01322_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "understanding. The Multi-Head attention (MHA) mechanisms repeats the self-attention computation multiple times in parallel. MHA uses multiple heads to attend to all the different aspects of an input sequence simultaneously. This allows it to provide high-quality results. However, this can be computationally expensive due to the parallel processing and can potentially lead to performance deterioration. Multi Query Attention (MQA) shares one key head and a single value head across all unique query" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2404_01322_rag__chunk_019> a kg:Chunk ;
