    kg:docId "2404.01322_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2404_01322_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "LoRA fine-tuning technique, focusing on memory efficiency. It incorporates quantisation, which involves reducing the precision of numerical values, during the adaption process. Instead of fine-tuning all 21 the weights of a pre-trained LLM, the LoRA technique is used to form LoRA adapters which are smaller matrices that can be fine-tuned to approximate the larger weight matrices. However, instead of low-rank approximation, QLoRA also applies quantisation to the weights of the LoRA adapters to fu" .

