    kg:docId "2404.01322_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2404_01322_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "summary of some MM-LLMs 6 Model Tuning columns: col1 row: col1=and comparison of the different training methods for MM-LLMs while Table 2 presents a summary of their characteristics. Model Open Fine- LLM Used Vision Model Used Source Tuneable LLaVA Yes Yes Vicuna CLIP ViT-L/14 Kosmos-1 and -2 Yes Yes Grounded image-text pairs to train an integrated model MiniGPT4 Yes Yes Vicuna Q-Former and CLIP ViT-G/14 mPLUG-OWL Yes Yes LLaMA-7B CLIP ViT-L/14 [/TABLE] in order to optimise the models performanc" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2406_09406_rag__chunk_013> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2406.09406_rag::chunk_013" ;
    kg:docId "2406.09406_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2406_09406_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "and tasks. This was achieved by mapping all modalities to discrete sets of tokens via modality-specific tokenizers and using a multimodal masked training objective [ 62 ]. We successfully scaled the training to 3 billion parameters and to 21 modalities and different datasets, without a degradation in performance compared to the existing expert single/few task models. This results in strong out-of-the-box capabilities as well new potential for multimodal interaction, generation, and retrieval, al" .

